[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read report by report, it holds three problems. Each now
has a ticket of its own in the [tracker](https://github.com/paulochoi/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues).

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} repo="paulochoi/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows" />

## How each report was placed

1. **Duplicates first.** The ticket system exports in overlapping pages, so some reports come twice. One id, one report.
2. **Tenant, not intake tag.** Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. The cause depends on the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), so the tag is shown but not used.
3. **Read the body.** A swapped day and month is the parser or the form hint. A date one day off, or a meeting that lands on different days in Lisbon and Toronto, is neither. The desk had already read those reports as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`); this page gives them their own problem instead of a footnote under the parser.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 will not close the other two. The booking-v3 hint keeps
producing month-first input, and a one-day shift is a time-zone bug, not a date-order bug.
</Callout>

## What changes for the desk

- Keep #4471 for the parser problem only.
- Route new booking-v3 form reports to the hint ticket, and one-day reports to the one-day ticket.
- A shared subject line is not a shared cause. Read the body before you merge.

